  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given length of latus-rectum of an ellipse is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></math> and&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Now we know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>",
